# Project Rules — CheckCopyRun

## 0. Workflow, AI Context & Task Lifecycle (CRITICAL)
- **Context bootstrap**: BEFORE starting ANY task, always read every file inside the `.ai/` directory (`.ai/todo.md`, `.ai/changelog.md`, `.ai/system_architecture.md`, etc.) to load the current project context.
- **Single active task**: Take into work ONLY the task listed in the `## 🎯 Текущая задача` block of `.ai/todo.md`. Never work on more than one task at a time.
- **Empty current task**: If `## 🎯 Текущая задача` is empty, agree on the next task with the user and move it there from the `## 📋 Очередь задач` block of `.ai/todo.md` first.
- **Task completion**: Once a task is finished AND tested, you MUST remove it from `.ai/todo.md` and record it in `.ai/changelog.md` with the current date and a short description of exactly what was done/changed in the code.

## 1. Tech Stack & Core Principles
- **Platform**: Windows 10+ only. Uses WinAPI (`SHGetKnownFolderPath`, `CryptProtectData`, `MonitorFromRect`), long paths, `explorer.exe`.
- **Language**: Python 3.12+ (`requires-python = ">=3.12"`). `ruff.toml` targets `py314`. Strict type hints are mandatory everywhere. PEP 8 + Ruff config (`line-length = 120`, `select = [E, W, F, I, N, UP, ANN, ASYNC, S, PTH, RUF]`).
- **UI**: `customtkinter` (on top of `tkinter`). No Flet, PyQt, Kivy, etc.
- **Images**: `Pillow` (icons, previews).
- **System**: `pywin32` (WinAPI — only where `ctypes` is inconvenient).
- **Tray (planned)**: `pystray` — only when the tray task is picked up; not used yet.
- **Build**: `Nuitka` via `build.py` (see §10).
- **Package manager**: `uv` (`pyproject.toml`, `[tool.uv] package = false`).
- **Linting**: `ruff` (`ruff.toml`). Before handing off a task — `ruff check` must pass.
- **Paradigm**: DRY, SRP. Absolute ban on global variables. Maximum indentation nesting depth: 3.
- **Dependencies**: only from `pyproject.toml`. Do not add a new library if the task is solvable with the standard library.

## 2. Localization (CRITICAL)
- **ALL** UI texts, inline comments, docstrings (Google style), log messages and commits MUST be written exclusively in **Russian**.
- Identifiers (function, class, variable names) MUST be in English, `snake_case` / `PascalCase` per standard.
- Dialog texts are coordinated with the product; changing them "along the way" without an explicit request is forbidden.

## 3. UI Layer (CustomTkinter / Tkinter)
- **Entry point**: `main.py` → `main() -> int` → `MainWindow(ctk.CTk)` → `app.mainloop()`. No other entrypoints.
- **Thread-safety**: Tkinter is not thread-safe. All UI updates MUST happen in the main thread via `self.after(0, fn)` (in `MainWindow` this is `scheduler`).
- **Long operations**: never run in the UI thread. Moved into `services/*` (usually `threading.Thread`), events returned via `scheduler`.
- **Routing**: `ui/navigation/router.py` is the only way to switch screens. Views are registered by factory, lazy, `on_show()` is the refresh point.
- **Main window is the orchestrator**: `MainWindow` owns `CopyService`, `RestoreService`, `Router`, `StatusBar`. Views do not create services and do not talk to them directly — only through `window.*`.
- **Dialogs**: only through the factory `ui/dialogs/setup_dialog` + `center_on_parent` + `bring_to_front`. Button styles — `ui/components/button.py` (`VARIANT_PRIMARY`, `VARIANT_SECONDARY`, `VARIANT_DANGER`).
- **Theme**: `ui/themes.py::apply_theme`. Do not hardcode theme colors — take them from `ui/palette.py`.
- **Fonts**: `ui/fonts.py::get_font` / `get_emoji_font`. Do not create `ctk.CTkFont` directly.
- **Icons**: `ui/components/image_utils.py::load_ctk_image` (Pillow → CTkImage). Emoji — via `get_emoji_font` (`Segoe UI Emoji`).
- **Async labels / background computations in UI**: if the result can become stale — use a generation counter (`_label_gen` in `ProfileView`), discard stale results.
- **Tooltip**: `ui/components/tooltip.py`. Hiding — on `<Leave>` + safety-polling; do not rely on a single event alone.

## 4. Services / Business Logic
- **Isolation from UI**: `services/*` MUST NOT import `customtkinter`, `tkinter`, `ui.*`. All interaction — via callbacks (`on_progress`, `on_done`, `on_error`).
- **Long operations**: `threading.Thread(daemon=True)` with an explicit `name` (for logs). Cancellation — `threading.Event` (`cancel_event`).
- **Scheduler**: injected from outside. In `MainWindow` — `lambda fn: self.after(0, fn)`; in tests — `lambda fn: fn()` (synchronous). Services MUST NOT call `after` themselves.
- **Errors**: internal — to the log (`logger.exception`), external — only via `on_error(message: str)`. No "silent" swallowing on the boundary.
- **No print()** — use `logger`.
- **State**: a service is stateless or holds the state of a single run. No global singletons.

## 5. Filesystem, CAS & Long Paths
- **Any I/O** MUST go through `core/long_io.py` (`open`, `copy2`, `makedirs`, `remove`, `replace`, `walk`, `stat`, `isdir`, `isfile`, `exists`, `listdir`, `scandir`, `disk_usage`). Direct `os.*` / `shutil.*` / `builtins.open` inside services are forbidden.
- **pathlib** — only for path manipulation (join, parent, name). For I/O — `long_io`.
- **Path comparison** — `os.path.abspath` + `os.path.normcase`, no `Path.resolve` (the latter does not support long paths). Ready helper — `core/paths.py::path_conflict_error`.
- **explorer.exe** does not understand the `\\?\` prefix — pass only the "plain" path to `explorer`. This is an OS limitation, not the app's.
- **Service folder `!CCRun`** in destination is an internal contract: `blobs/`, `states/`, `current.json`, `hashes.json`. The structure is part of CAS and must not be changed without a migration.
- **Atomicity**: any `!CCRun` file (and `settings.dat`) MUST be written via `.tmp` + `os.replace`. Intermediate state must not be visible to other processes.
- **Deleting blobs** — only via `BlobStore.gc(keep)` after diffing against the set of used hashes. Direct `unlink` of a blob is forbidden.

## 6. Settings, Secrets & Persistence
- **Settings**: `%USERPROFILE%/Documents/CheckCopyRun/settings.dat`, DPAPI encryption (`services/system/dpapi.py`). Bound to the current Windows user.
- **Secrets**: only via `os.getenv()`. No secrets in code or logs.
- **Migrations**: old fields must not crash — `_from_dict` reads with defaults, unknown keys ignored.
- **Constants**: all "magic" numbers and strings — `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` in `config/constants.py` or in the owning module.

## 7. Logging
- **Module**: `utils/logger.py::get_logger(__name__)` in every module.
- **File**: `Documents/CheckCopyRun/log/app.log`, `RotatingFileHandler`, UTF-8.
- **Levels**: `debug` — diagnostics, `info` — significant events, `warning` — unexpected but not fatal, `error` — with `exc_info=True` for exceptions.
- **No print()**. Neither in code nor in tests (for debugging — `logger.debug`, `pytest -s`).

## 8. Code Quality
- **Exceptions**: only specific (`except OSError as e:`, `except ValueError as e:`). Broad `except Exception:` is forbidden in business logic; on boundaries (top-level callback, background thread, `scheduler`) it is allowed only with `logger.error(..., exc_info=True)`.
- **Context managers**: `with open(...)`, `with long_io.open(...)`. No manual `close()`.
- **Imports**: sorted by Ruff (`known-first-party = ["config", "core", "services", "ui", "utils"]`). Absolute imports, no relative (except within a single package).
- **Docstrings**: Google style, in Russian, only for public entities. Internal — optional.
- **Magic numbers**: forbidden. Everything — in `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
- **Nesting**: maximum 3 levels. Deeper — extract into a function.

## 9. Testing
- **Framework**: `pytest`. Config — `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` in `pyproject.toml` (`testpaths = ["tests"]`, `pythonpath = ["."]`).
- **What we test**: `services/**` and pure functions (`core/paths.py`, `core/long_io.py`, `services/selection_model.py`, `services/cas/destination_state.py`, `services/startup_check.py`, etc.).
- **What we do not test**: CustomTkinter rendering, Tk widgets, real `filedialog`, real `explorer`. The UI layer is tested manually.
- **Isolation from Tk**: tests MUST NOT import `customtkinter`. If a `scheduler` is needed — `lambda fn: fn()`.
- **Fixtures**: `tests/conftest.py` — `src`, `dst`, `run_copy`, `run_restore`. For new scenarios add fixtures there as well.
- **Naming**: `test_<target_function>_<test_condition>_<expected_outcome>`.
- **Windows-only tests**: mark with `pytest.mark.skipif(not sys.platform == "win32", ...)`.

## 10. Build & Distribution
- **Build**: `uv run build.py` (folder), `uv run build.py --onefile` (single `.exe`), `uv run build.py --debug` (with console).
- **Artifact**: `build/CCRun.exe` (or `build/CCRun.dist/CCRun.exe`). Exe name — `CCRun`; product name — `Check, Copy & Run`; company — `CheckCopyRun`. Version — from `config/constants.py::APP_VERSION`.
- **Icon**: `assets/icon.ico`. Embedded via `--windows-icon-from-ico`, copied as data via `--include-data-dir`.
- **Entrypoint**: `main.py`. Nuitka builds exactly this file.
- **Not shipped**: `tests/`, `pytest`, `ruff`, `mypy`, `pip`, `setuptools` — listed in `build.py::_NOFOLLOW_IMPORTS`.
